Show experimental cores in the Core Updater by default.

The Linux aarch64 buildbot only publishes nightly builds, and a large part of
that set is flagged is_experimental in the core info files. With the upstream
default of false the Core Downloader silently filters those entries out, so on
this target the list is a fraction of what the buildbot actually carries -- the
user has to find the toggle under Settings -> Network before the downloader is
of much use.

This is only a listing filter; it downloads nothing extra on its own.

--- a/config.def.h	2026-09-20 13:32:50.761651965 +0700
+++ b/config.def.h	2026-09-20 13:32:50.770652291 +0700
@@ -1469,7 +1469,7 @@
 #define DEFAULT_STDIN_CMD_ENABLE false
 
 #define DEFAULT_NETWORK_BUILDBOT_AUTO_EXTRACT_ARCHIVE true
-#define DEFAULT_NETWORK_BUILDBOT_SHOW_EXPERIMENTAL_CORES false
+#define DEFAULT_NETWORK_BUILDBOT_SHOW_EXPERIMENTAL_CORES true
 
 /* Automatically create a backup whenever a core is
  * updated via the online updater
